      <activity id="92a9ad91-2bb8-5ba5-b441-1cc701af6ed7" activityNameId="130b7e24-615e-54e9-9f19-34109bbaa2fe" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Low active radioactive waste</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Low active radioactive waste
The module is oversimplified and shall be considered only as a preliminary description of the storage of low radioactive waste in surface or trench depositories. (The current version of the study has given priority to nuclear depositories for high and intermediate level as well as long-lived radioactive waste.) No leackage is accounted for. Hence, this module may not reflect specific situations. There have been reported leakages from surface depositories, which are continuously monitored. These cases should be rapidly taken care of by removing the leaking object and seal the waste again. A careful modelling of these waste depositories shall be accomplished together with the expected completion of the waste modelling in the next edition of ecoinvent.;
UUID: 3c080289-ef2f-4848-ae59-d9938a1917ac
The module includes only the land use and the energy used for digging. 
Location: Generic.
Technology: Unspecified.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_3c080289-ef2f-4848-ae59-d9938a1917ac.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
